\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By J. Edward Moreno and Reuters \par \uc2 502 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 March 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LABOR\par \par \uc2 Unions End Fight\par \par \uc2 With Starbucks Board\par \par \uc2 A coalition of labor unions said Tuesday that it had ended its boardroom fight with \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  after the coffeehouse chain agreed to negotiate labor agreements, a sign of progress after years of tumultuous relations between the company and its organized workers.\par \par \uc2 The Strategic Organizing Center union alliance pulled its slate of three board candidates about a week before a March 11 shareholder vote on the 11-member board. The announcement comes more than two years into a campaign that has unionized nearly 400 \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the alliance said it was ''time to acknowledge the progress that has been made and to allow the company and its workers to focus on moving forward.''\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers began organizing in 2021 with three Buffalo-area stores. Since that campaign began, the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  has filed numerous complaints accusing \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  of taking steps to resist organizing efforts, which the company has denied. According to the union alliance, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has spent more than $240 million to quash union efforts. The two parties have also sued each other over the union's right to use a logo that resembles the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  logo.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and the union that represents its workers, Workers United, whose parent is part of the labor alliance, said late last month that they were beginning discussions about a ''foundational framework'' to help reach labor agreements and resolve litigation over the union's use of the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  logo.\par \par \uc2 The union alliance said in a statement on Tuesday that it had since had ''meaningful dialogue'' with shareholders who it says are optimistic that the company is focused on repairing its relationship with its workers. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  shareholders last year passed a resolution directing the company to commission an assessment of its labor practices.\par \par \uc2 ''Our board's focus remains on driving long-term value for all stakeholders, including partners, shareholders, customers and farmers,'' \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  said in a statement on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 J. EDWARD MORENO\par \par \uc2 RETAIL\par \par \uc2 Target to Introduce\par \par \uc2 Paid Membership\par \par \uc2 Target on Tuesday reported higher holiday-quarter earnings on a smaller-than-expected sales decline and predicted that annual comparable sales would come in largely above Wall Street expectations, sending its shares up 12 percent.\par \par \uc2 The mass merchandiser is banking on same-day services, product launches and a new membership program to boost spending at its stores.\par \par \uc2 Target plans to launch a membership feature called Target Circle 360 next month, which would offer shoppers unlimited same-day delivery, said \uc2 Brian Cornell\uc2 , the chief executive.\par \par \uc2 Target\uc2  reported adjusted earnings of $2.98 per share in the fourth quarter, compared to $1.89 per share in the same period a year earlier. Analysts on average expected $2.42 per share, according to \uc2 LSEG\uc2  estimates.\par \par \uc2 Online sales fell 0.7 percent during the fourth quarter, an improvement from the 6 percent decline in the previous quarter. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY BRENDAN MCDERMID/REUTERS) This article appeared in print on page B2. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240306ek360004q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
