\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Benjamin Mullin and The Associated Press \par \uc2 555 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 February 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MEDIA\par \par \uc2 Complex, a BuzzFeed Unit,Is Sold for $108.6 Million\par \par \uc2 BuzzFeed\uc2  said on Wednesday that it was selling Complex -- a media start-up that covers streetwear and pop culture -- at a significant discount from its purchase price.\par \par \uc2 The buyer is Ntwrk, an e-commerce company backed by LiveNation Entertainment and Main Street Advisors, which is paying $108.6 million for Complex. It is also paying \uc2 BuzzFeed\uc2  $5.7 million to cover severance expenses of Complex employees whom \uc2 BuzzFeed\uc2  is laying off, and other costs.\par \par \uc2 BuzzFeed\uc2  said it was laying off 16 percent of its remaining workers, a move it expects will save $23 million annually. It is not selling First We Feast, the internet brand associated with Complex behind the popular ''Hot Ones'' interview series about hot wings.\par \par \uc2 Jonah Peretti\uc2 , above right, \uc2 BuzzFeed\uc2 's co-founder and chief executive, said in a statement that selling Complex was ''an important strategic step'' for the company.\par \par \uc2 BuzzFeed\uc2 , which has suffered a steep discount in its valuation since it went public in 2021, is selling Complex to pay off over $60 million in debt. \uc2 BuzzFeed\uc2  said in a financial filing that it had $150 million in debt due in 2026 and an additional $33.8 million from a line of credit.\par \par \uc2 Complex, which generated over $55 million of revenue last year, is being sold for more than the market capitalization of its owner, \uc2 BuzzFeed\uc2 , which is about $31 million. \uc2 BuzzFeed\uc2  acquired Complex in 2021 for about $294 million in cash and stock.\par \par \uc2 Aaron Levant, who will be Complex's new chief executive, said in a statement that the deal would create ''the definitive global content, commerce and experiential platform of convergence culture.'' BENJAMIN MULLIN\par \par \uc2 LABOR\par \par \uc2 U.A.W. Reaches DealAt Biggest Ford Factory\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Ford Motor Company\uc2  and the \uc2 United Automobile Workers union\uc2  have reached a tentative agreement on a local contract at the company's largest and most profitable factory, averting the threat of a strike.\par \par \uc2 The union said last week said that nearly 9,000 workers at the Kentucky Truck Plant in Louisville would walk picket lines starting Friday if the contract dispute was not resolved.\par \par \uc2 But the U.A.W. said in a statement on Wednesday that a deal had been reached.\par \par \uc2 The tentative agreement addresses health and safety issues, ergonomics, the company's efforts to reduce the number of skilled trades workers and other issues, the union said.\par \par \uc2 The plant, one of two Ford factories in Louisville, makes heavy-duty F-Series pickup trucks and the Ford Excursion and Lincoln Navigator large S.U.V.s, all hugely profitable vehicles.\par \par \uc2 A strike at the sprawling plant would have been the second in the past year. In October, U.A.W. workers shut down the plant during national contract negotiations that ended with large pay raise.\par \par \uc2 Workers had been without a local contract for five months, the U.A.W. said.\par \par \uc2 Ford's chief executive, \uc2 Jim Farley\uc2 , told an analysts' conference this month that last fall's strike changed Ford's relationship with the U.A.W. to the point where the company would ''think carefully'' about where it builds future vehicles. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY MICHELLE GROSKOPF FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) This article appeared in print on page B2. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240222ek2m0004r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{