\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Daily News Employees Stage One-Day Walkout\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katie Robertson \par \uc2 314 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 January 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Newsroom workers at The Daily News Union, which formed in 2021, are in negotiations for their first contract.\par \par \uc2 Journalists at The New York Daily News walked off the job on Thursday for the first time in more than three decades.\par \par \uc2 Newsroom workers at The Daily News Union, which formed in 2021, are in negotiations for their first contract. The union called a one-day work stoppage to protest staffing cuts, as well as a new policy that requires workers to get advance approval for overtime.\par \par \uc2 The Daily News, founded in 1919, was once one of the largest newspapers in the country by circulation. But in recent years, the paper has been hollowed out by ownership changes and staffing cuts as it struggled against ever-declining circulation and dwindling revenue.\par \par \uc2 In 2021, its parent company, \uc2 Tribune Publishing\uc2 , was purchased by \uc2 Alden Global Capital\uc2 , an investment firm that has bought up hundreds of newspapers across the country, acquiring a reputation along the way for making deep cuts to newsrooms.\par \par \uc2 About a third of union members have left The Daily News since spring 2022, with membership now at 54 people, according to the union.\par \par \uc2 ''In reality, we're being crushed for cash,'' Michael Gartland, a Daily News reporter and union steward, said in a statement. ''As a result, staff is diminished, which means our ability to cover the city is diminished.''\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for \uc2 Alden Global Capital\uc2  did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The last work stoppage at The Daily News was a five-month strike in 1990 and 1991.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Daily News journalists plan to picket outside a co-working space that now serves at their temporary office. The Daily News permanently closed its newsroom in Lower Manhattan in 2020.\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page B2. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240126ek1q0003j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
